Follow these simple steps to bake bakery-quality treats at home.  

**What You Need:**  
1 Package Chocolate Chip Cookie Mix.  
    Base Dry Mix includes: Flour, Sugars, Leavening, Salt, etc.  
---
**Equipment**  
* Medium mixing bowl & Hand Mixer  
   or Stand mixer  
* Spatula  
* Large cookie sheet or sheet pan  
* Parchment paper  
  
**Wet Ingredients (To Add)**  
* Unsalted Butter: 3/4 cup (1 1/2 sticks, 170 grams), room temp (See Baker's Tip)  
* Large Eggs: 2, room temp (see Baker's Tip)  
* Vanilla Extract: 2 tsp, (9 mL)  

**Baking Instructions**  
1. Prep:  
Preheat your oven to 325°F (160°C). Line a large cookie sheet or sheet pan with parchment paper. This will help with removal.  
<img src="{{ '/assets/img/square-pan-with-parchment.png' | relative_url }}" class="recipe-photo" alt="Square pan with parchment">  
2. Mix Wet Ingredients:  
Add room temp butter to a mixing bowl and mix on medium speed until light and fluffy, for about 2 minutes. Mix in the eggs and vanilla until smooth.  
3. Combine Mix:  
Add the entire contents of the Chocolate Chip Cookie Mix Pouch into the bowl. Mix dry ingredients in at low speed or with a spatula until just combined and no dry flour remains. Do not over mix.  
4. Nake the cookies:  

5. Bake:  
Pour Blondie batter into the prepared pan and spread evenly.  
Place in the oven and bake for 30-35 minutes, or until the blondies are golden brown and set (use a cake tester, thin blade knife or toothpick inserted into the center. Should see moist crumbs attached, not wet batter). Do not over bake.  
6. Cool & Enjoy:  
For best texture and taste, allow the Blondies to **cool to room temperature fully** before slicing and serving. Use the parchment paper sling to carefully remove the blondies to a serving plate or cutting board. Slice into desired sized bars.  
7. Storing:  
Room Temperature & Fridge: Store in an airtight container for up to 3 days at room temperature or up to 5 days in the fridge.  
Freezer: Wrap the cooled whole slab or individual slices of Blondies in plastic wrap and place inside an airtight container. Store in freezer for up to 3 months. Thaw overnight in the fridge, or for a couple hours at room temperature, before serving.  
---
> **Baker's Tips:**  
For an extra gourmet touch, sprinkle a light pinch of flaky sea salt over the warm Blondies right as they come out of the oven.  
**Having all ingredients at the same temperature will produce a smooth batter and best results.  
**Slice butter sticks into small pats to speed up warming to room temperature.  
**Place eggs in a bowl of warm water to speed up warming to room temperature.  
**A metal pan is best. Glass and ceramic conduct heat more slowly than metals (the edges will dry out and the center will take longer to bake fully). If glass/ceramic is all that is available, increase the baking time anywhere from 5-10 minutes.  
